# NEVER COMMITTED.  `secrets/` is 0700 and holds every generated value;
# `.env` holds the rendered pin block and the database passwords.
#
# The mode on `secrets/` is 0700 owned by the OPERATOR, not by root: it holds
# root-owned per-service files, and the operator has to be able to traverse it
# or compose cannot read any env_file (MEASURED, NOM-258 — see gen-secrets.sh).
secrets/
.env
.runtime/
backups/
config/authelia/users.yml
config/image-facts.yaml.bak
*.bak
.backup-keys-confirmed

# GENERATED, NEVER COMMITTED — and this one is load-bearing, not tidiness.
#
# MEASURED (NOM-258, 2026-10-18): three `security-report-*/invariants.txt`
# files were committed, and invariant I6 scans every file `git ls-files`
# reports for banned strings.  A saved report PRINTS I6's own description,
# which names the banned browser sandbox flag — so the report contained it,
# and I6 FAILED on a clean clone of HEAD.  CI red for no reason but the repo
# shipping its own scan output.  The working tree passed only because someone
# had deleted those files locally without committing the deletion, which is
# the worst version of this: green where the build runs, red where anyone
# else checks it out.
#
# This comment deliberately does NOT quote the flag.  It was written with the
# literal first, and I6 failed on THIS file — correctly.  The fix is prose
# that describes the string, not a third entry in I6's self-exclusion list.
security-report-*/
support-bundle-*.tar.gz
drill-log.txt
install.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
